# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT backed up to GitHub, and why.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 7.2 GB of public reference data: hg38 FASTA (3.1 GB), GENCODE GTF (3.2 GB),
# ENCODE eCLIP files, CisBP-RNA motif PWMs. GitHub's hard per-file limit is
# 100 MB and these exceed it by 30x.
#
# This is not a backup gap: `data/source_manifest.json` records the URL, byte
# size, SHA-256, retrieval date and license of every asset, and the following
# command re-fetches and verifies all of them, failing loudly on any mismatch:
#
#     motifcheck validate-sources
#
# Provenance lives in the manifest; bulk reproducible data does not.
data/external/

# Snakemake's internal scheduling state and metadata cache. Purely transient;
# rebuilt on the next run. The human-readable execution logs ARE tracked.
.snakemake/
.bench/

# Python bytecode and packaging noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Generic logs outside the tracked logs/ directory
*.log
!logs/*.log
# Generated FASTA index for the toy test fixture
tests/fixtures/*.fai
